/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlassess","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAssess","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, an assessment application should assess all notes without a cue child element, and not assess any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"note with a cue child element. The assess type allows this default assessment to be overridden for individual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notes. The optional player and time-only attributes restrict the type to apply to a single player or set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times through a repeated section, respectively. If missing, the type applies to all players or all times"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the repeated section, respectively. The player attribute references the id attribute of a player"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element defined within the matching score-part."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAssess","kind":"identifier"}]}}}